&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Figma is growing our team of passionate creatives and builders on a mission to make design accessible to all. Figma’s platform helps teams bring ideas to life—whether you&#39;re brainstorming, creating a prototype, translating designs into code, or iterating with AI. From idea to product, Figma empowers teams to streamline workflows, move faster, and work together in real time from anywhere in the world. If you&#39;re excited to shape the future of design and collaboration, join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Figma is growing our team of passionate people on a mission to make design accessible to all.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.figma.com/blog/meet-us-in-the-browser/&quot;&gt; Born on the Web&lt;/a&gt;, Figma helps entire product teams&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.figma.com/blog/introducing-figjam/&quot;&gt; brainstorm&lt;/a&gt;, create, test, and ship better designs, together. From great products to long-lasting companies, we believe that nothing great is made alone - come&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.figma.com/blog/inside-maker-week-more-than-a-hackathon/&quot;&gt; make&lt;/a&gt; with us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Figma is looking for a Director, SMB Sales (EMEA) to join our growing Global Commercial organization. As Director of SMB Sales, EMEA, you&#39;ll lead a team of frontline managers and Account Executives responsible for helping growing businesses adopt Figma&#39;s Organization and Enterprise plans. Reporting to the VP of Commercial Sales, you&#39;ll play a critical role in scaling a high-volume, specialized sales motion while partnering closely with leaders across the Americas and JAPAC to drive consistency, share best practices, and evolve how we serve SMB customers globally. This is an opportunity to shape the next chapter of one of Figma&#39;s fastest-growing businesses, leading a talented team while influencing strategy across Sales, Marketing, Operations, Enablement, and Product. At Figma, we value leaders who think creatively, challenge the status quo, and build teams that consistently raise the bar for customer experience and business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full time role that can be held from one of our EMEA hubs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do at Figma:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and inspire a team of frontline managers and Account Executives, building a high-performing culture focused on coaching, accountability, and customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale the EMEA SMB business by driving operational excellence across forecasting, pipeline management, inspection, and execution against revenue goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with SMB leaders across the Americas and JAPAC to build a globally consistent sales motion, sharing best practices and raising execution standards across regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, hire, and develop exceptional sales leaders while building a strong internal pipeline of future Mid-Market leaders and second-line managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach managers through forecast reviews, pipeline inspections, deal strategy, call coaching, and performance management to improve both team execution and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to identify opportunities, test new strategies, and continuously improve the SMB sales motion, including territory design, pipeline generation, productivity, and conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Operations, Enablement, Marketing, Solutions Consulting, Customer Experience, and Product to influence the evolution of the SMB business and improve how we serve customers globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an executive sponsor for strategic customer opportunities while representing the voice of EMEA in the continued evolution of Figma&#39;s global SMB strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience leading SaaS sales organizations, including at least 4 years in sales management. You’ve managed frontline leaders and spent at least 2 years in a second-line leadership role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve led distributed sales teams across multiple countries and understand the differences between EMEA markets. Comfortable balancing long-term strategy with the realities of day-to-day execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Built and scaled teams of Sales Managers and Account Executives in a high-growth company. Ideally, you also have experience with SMB or Commercial SaaS sales, particularly in a product-led growth business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know how to coach leaders, develop talent, and create inclusive teams that perform consistently. You’ve exceeded revenue targets while improving forecasting and building dependable sales processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident using data to make decisions and have worked closely with Marketing, Operations, Enablement, Product, and other go-to-market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;While it’s not required, it’s an added plus if you also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using or working with Figma, or other UX/UI experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional European language fluency (e.g. French, German, Spanish)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Command of the Message or MEDDIC/MEDDICC sales methodology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background scaling teams across multiple EMEA markets simultaneously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Figma, one of our values is Grow as you go. We believe in hiring smart, curious people who are excited to learn and develop their skills. If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with the points outlined in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Figma we celebrate and support our differences. We know employing a team rich in diverse thoughts, experiences, and opinions allows our employees, our product and our community to flourish. Figma is an &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/EEOC_KnowYourRights_screen_reader_10_20.pdf&quot;&gt;equal opportunity workplace&lt;/a&gt; - we are dedicated to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity/expression, veteran status&lt;strong&gt;, &lt;/strong&gt;or any other characteristic protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will work to ensure individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to apply for a role, participate in the interview process, perform essential job functions, and receive other benefits and privileges of employment. If you require accommodation, please reach out to &lt;a ---------- These modifications enable an individual with a disability to have an equal opportunity not only to get a job, but successfully perform their job tasks to the same extent as people without disabilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Examples of accommodations include but are not limited to:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holding interviews in an accessible location&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enabling closed captioning on video conferencing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring all written communication be compatible with screen readers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Changing the mode or format of interviews&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To ensure the integrity of our hiring process and facilitate a more personal connection, we require all candidates keep their cameras on during video interviews. Additionally, if hired you will be required to attend in person onboarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By applying for this job, the candidate acknowledges and agrees that any personal data contained in their application or supporting materials will be processed in accordance with &lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.figma.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.figma.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Figma&#39;s Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application limits:&lt;/strong&gt; To help candidates focus on the opportunities most relevant to their skills and experience, Figma limits the number and frequency of applications. These limits apply to all roles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates may submit up to 5 applications during any rolling 30-day period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates may not reapply to the same role while an application is active or within 90 days of receiving a rejection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Once the applicable days has passed, candidates are welcome to apply again.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Doctolib&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Doctolib Connect is a secure medical communication app designed for healthcare professionals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than 1M healthcare professionals use Doctolib Connect to discuss and coordinate patient care with colleagues both within and beyond their organizational walls. Today, Doctolib Connect is the largest medical network in Europe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since 2013, Doctolib has been striving for a healthier world by providing new-generation technology. With more than 2,800 employees across France, Italy, Germany and the Netherlands, Doctolib improves the daily lives of healthcare professionals and serves more than 80 million Europeans, offering a fast, frictionless, and secure journey for all their care needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Fullstack Engineer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;to join the &lt;strong&gt;Doctolib Connect &lt;/strong&gt;team in &lt;strong&gt;Amsterdam, Netherlands&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Fullstack Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, your mission will be to work on &lt;strong&gt;web features&lt;/strong&gt; for our secure medical communication solutions that enable healthcare professionals to discuss and coordinate patient care with colleagues both within and beyond their organizational walls. You will be working in a feature team developing a product that powers Europe&#39;s largest medical network with over 1M healthcare professionals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working in the tech team at Doctolib involves building innovative products and features to improve the daily lives of care teams and patients. We work in feature teams in an agile environment, while collaborating with product, design, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities include but are not limited to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frontend (React): building and owning web features, reviewing code and setting quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backend and APIs (Java): API-focused work that supports the frontend and the features it owns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical leadership and delivery ownership: estimates, delivery plans, breaking down projects, giving the team context, accountability for results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration and team practices: working with the PM and Designer, supporting ways of working and processes, mentoring other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing the full development lifecycle, including stakeholder communication and production issue debugging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About our tech environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our solutions are built on a single fully cloud-native platform that supports web and mobile app interfaces, multiple languages, and is adapted to the country and healthcare specialty requirements. To address these challenges, we are modularizing our platform run in a distributed architecture through reusable components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our stack is composed of React, TypeScript, Java, Rails, Python, Kotlin, Swift, and React Native.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We leverage AI ethically across our products to empower patients and health professionals. Discover our AI vision &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.doctolib.com/ai-careers/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; and learn about our first AI hackathon &lt;a href=&quot;https://medium.com/doctolib/building-for-healthcare-our-first-ai-hackathon-aa9d10d1a250&quot;&gt;here!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before you read on: if you don&#39;t have the exact profile described below, but you feel this job description matches your skill set, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years experience working as fullstack software engineer on user facing applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience with React, Typescript and one or more of our backend technologies (Java, Rails...)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience running software on cloud infrastructure, ideally AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience working with database technologies, preferably JPA, MySQL, MongoDB and Elasticsearch/Opensearch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy figuring out why things work, not just that they work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re fluent in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension scheme through our partner Allianz&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;27 days of annual leave per year (and the ability to accrue more days on your work anniversary!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from abroad for up to 10 days per year thanks to our flexibility days policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enrollment in Doctolib&#39;s long-term employee value sharing plan called DoctoGrowth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free mental health and coaching services through our partner Moka.care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast and lunch plan every day on-site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bike lease scheme with our partner Lease a Bike, 35% price below the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discounted membership with Urban Sports Club&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous training programs on all key competencies (English, soft skills, expertise)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reimbursement of public transportation if you live outside the Amsterdam highway ring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parent Care Program:&amp;nbsp; Various initiatives supporting parenthood, including 100% paid parental leave up to 16 weeks, including bonuses, for mothers and up to 5 weeks for the co-parent, flexible return and 3 days of leave per year for child sickness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relocation support for international mobilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The interview process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruiter Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coding Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;System Design Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Behavioral Interview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offer!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Doctolib, we are committed to improving access to healthcare for everyone. This translates into our recruitment process. We evaluate candidates based solely on qualifications and motivation, without any form of discrimination.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The more diverse ideas are heard, the more our product will truly improve healthcare for all. You are welcome to apply to Doctolib, regardless of your gender, religion, age, sexual orientation, ethnicity, disability.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To ensure equal opportunities, we invite you to exclude personal information (e.g. pictures, age) from your applications. If you require any accommodation, please let us know for support during the hiring process. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Join us in building the healthcare we all dream of!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;All information provided is processed by Doctolib for application management. For data processing details, click&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://media.doctolib.com/image/upload/v1678356494/legal/Career-Privacy-Policy-Feb-23-EN.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please contact hr.dataprivacy(at)doctolib.com for inquiries or to exercise your rights.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flexport:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flexport, we believe global trade can move the human race forward. That’s why it’s our mission to make global commerce so easy there will be more of it. We’re shaping the future of a $10T industry with solutions powered by innovative technology and exceptional people. Today, companies of all sizes—from emerging brands to Fortune 500s—use Flexport technology to move more than $19B of merchandise across 112 countries a year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recent global supply chain crisis has put Flexport center stage as we continue to play a pivotal role in how goods move around the world. We are proud to have the support of the best investors in the game who believe in our mission, solutions and people. Ready to tackle global challenges that impact business, society, and the environment? Come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your responsibilities as a &lt;strong&gt;Director, EMEA Ocean Operations&lt;/strong&gt; include, but are not limited to the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a leadership team of Senior Managers and Managers, who in turn run Ocean Operations teams across EMEA. You are accountable for organisation design, hiring plans and succession planning at every level beneath you. You build a culture of high performance and psychological safety, and you make sure the organisation scales with the business rather than just adding people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end EMEA ocean gateway operations (FCL and LCL) across all markets, both insourced and partner-operated countries. You set one operating standard for how work is done, and you decide where it makes sense for local markets to differ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and deliver the multi-year EMEA ocean strategy and the planning cycles that support it (biannual planning and quarterly check-ins). You separate what the core operation needs to keep running well from what is expansion, and you turn that into clear choices on investment, team size and priorities, aligned with EMEA operations goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and drive the EMEA ocean automation roadmap with your teams. You decide where to remove manual work first, so that volume growth does not need proportional growth in manual work, and you work with Product, Engineering and Operational Excellence to deliver it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the senior operations voice to EMEA Operational Excellence, Global Product and Engineering. You turn operational pain points across EMEA into clear product priorities, and you help decide what gets built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report to the EMEA Head of Operations and serve as a member of the EMEA Senior Leadership Team. You help set the direction for EMEA as a whole, not just for your own area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with EMEA commercial leadership (GMs) and global operations leaders in other regions. You make sure commercial promises and operational reality match, you flag deal and delivery risk early, and you share what works across regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold executive-level relationships with key clients, carriers and partner operators. You lead major escalations, negotiate service commitments with partners, and represent EMEA operations in client business reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to find the biggest bottlenecks and root causes across markets, not just fix individual cases. You set the metrics the organisation runs on and make sure leaders at every level are held to them in regular reviews (weekly, monthly and quarterly business reviews).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the long-term capacity plan. You work with Operations Excellence and Finance on staffing models that cope with seasonal peaks and multi-year growth, including the balance between insourced teams and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the P&amp;amp;L and operational health of EMEA ocean gateway operations. You set the financial discipline for your area, stop revenue and cost leakage at scale (for example, billing accessorials), and make sure your leaders do the same in their teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prerequisites:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree in Logistics, Supply Chain Management or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of measurable business results, including quantified impact on quality, productivity, efficiency and customer service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in cross-border supply chains, logistics and/or freight forwarding, with ocean freight experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of people management experience, including managing managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in customer-facing roles, with experience managing senior client or partner relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running operations across several countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technology (and AI) first mindset, comfortable in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent English; ideally other European languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent technical skills (e.g. Claude, N8N, Looker, Excel)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owner&#39;s mindset and strong discipline across the whole organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer obsession, with high standards as a point of pride&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An operator at heart who removes waste and redesigns processes for lean, scalable efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dives into metrics to fix root causes while delivering the short-term wins that stabilise operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds trust through transparent, concise communication and encourages the team to challenge the status quo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s in it for you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An opportunity to contribute to one of the fastest-growing companies, where you’ll have the chance to create a global impact while being a part of a&amp;nbsp; thriving multinational environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily catered lunches incl. vegetarian options, breakfast, snacks and soft drinks available in our office on daily basis&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commute expenses: Flexport will cover&amp;nbsp; home-office commuting costs for employees living outside of Amsterdam&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Amazing office in the heart of Amsterdam.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 working days as vacation days based on full time employment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health insurance: Flexport offers a collective health insurance plan including a basic package and any available additional packages. Your monthly premium is fully paid by Flexport.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A defined pension contribution scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity program: every team member becomes a shareholder, aligning our success with yours. As a private company in a multi-trillion dollar industry, you have a direct stake in our collective growth and success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program through Aetna Resources for Living: Flexport provides an employer-sponsored program at no cost to you and your household members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental leave benefit: Flexport is here to support you and your families in one of the most important times in life – the birth of a child! Our parental leave program allows both mothers and partners to take time off from work for pregnancy, childbirth, and to bond with your new child.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
